  "answer": "This request has been filed before. Tickets PowerToys#34950 (Window Masking) and PowerToys#48566 (Restrict App Sharing) both ask for a way to hide specific windows from screen sharing, recording and screenshots, using WDA_EXCLUDEFROMCAPTURE. PowerToys does not offer this feature today. Both tickets were closed as duplicates: #34950 was pointed to #13035, and #48566 to #46333. A commenter on #34950 questioned whether #13035 is the right tracking issue, because it is about inactive window appearance. Subscribe to #46333 for updates on the request. Until a feature ships, the open-source tools winhider (github.com/[user]/winhider) and Invisiwind (github.com/[user]/Invisiwind), mentioned in #34950, do similar things. They do not detect newly opened windows. Alternatively, share a single window or monitor rather than your whole screen."
